From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Mar 25 23:04:36 1997
From: Casey Spangler <spang () probita ! com>
Date: Tue, 25 Mar 1997 23:04:36 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Problem running dtadvfs
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078609810641

Original post, edited:

I've been trying to run the GUI for the AdvFS Utilities, dtadvfs. The
splash screen comes up, followed by the "connect hosts" window. The name of
the local machine comes up in the window. When I try to connect, I get
"failed to make agent connection to host." 

Sorry for the lateness of the summary. Thanks to all who replied,
particularly:
Miguel Mena <migi@zuo.dec.com>
Dejan Muhamedagic <muja@galeb.etf.bg.ac.yu>
who hit it right on the head. The solution was to fully qualify the
hostname in /var/opt/advfsd/socket/hosts.allow.

BTW, several wrote that the real utility is dxadvfs. On my machine, dxadvfs
is a symbolic link to dtadvfs.
