From: Trevor Stott <trevor.stott () sheridanc ! on ! ca>
Date: Mon, 17 Mar 1997 19:14:01 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Best setup for swap
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078609810441


Hello Managers,
	I received a number of responses regarding the best setup for swap.  I think 
I can summarize it best by saying that 2 to 3 times is a good rule but not 
manditory.  If your running large applications you can end up needing as much 
as 5 or 6 times the amount of physical memory in swap but only in cases where 
RAM is not abundant.  If RAM is plentiful and swap usage is down there is no 
reason to increase the amount of swap.

					Thanks to all those who replied!

