From tru64-unix-managers  Sat Mar 15 10:28:53 1997
From: Dominik Uehlinger <uehlinger () mph ! unibe ! ch>
Date: Sat, 15 Mar 1997 10:28:53 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary OSF 1.3 ==> DU 4.0B
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078609810410

This is a late summary - after all I first had to check if it really was
so simple as it looked at the beginning - and it was.

The new installation of DU 4.0B on an old DEC 3000-400 is straight
forward without any problems. 

The only problem encountered was with the firmware upgrade. I ordered a
new SROM chip from DIGITAL (only necessary for a DEC 3000-400) and
replaced the SROM. The result of the replacement was that the machine
forgot that it was a computer (blank). The following method finally
worked:
1. Upgrade firmware to the highest secure level (6.0)
2. Replace SROM
3. Upgrade firmware to the final level (6.8)

Many thanks to Paul Henderson (henderson@unx.dec.com) who convinced me
to directly install 4.0 since the installation procedure has been much
simplified (graphical configuration applications) as compared with 3.x


