Dear Gurus,

My question was: is there any problem in removing the /var/adm/wtmp file?

Answer: basically, NO.

However, if the wtmp file is removed and not re-created, then of course
there will be no accounting, but also the "w" and "who" commands won't
work any longer. It is therefore a bad idea.

What I did was therefore "cat /dev/null > /var/adm/wtmp"

