first the printer is a tcp/ip printer not conected to a host , it is
like a station on the network, so at the Release notes of the 4.0A page
2-13 there is a discription of how to configure such printer.
I add the line hplaser5m  9100/tcp to the /etc/services file,
done the rcinet restart, and add the ct=tcp and lp=@wizhp5m/hplaser5m
and the printcap look like :

hp5m|lp:\
