From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Mar 10 23:45:28 1997
From: Tim Mooney <mooney () dogbert ! cc ! ndsu ! NoDak ! edu>
Date: Mon, 10 Mar 1997 23:45:28 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: AlphaServer 2100 -> 2100A gotchas?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078609810268


The original question is attached at the end of this message.

I received responses from:

Christophe Wolfhugel <wolf@pasteur.fr>
alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com
Karl Marble <marblek@ci.worcester.ma.us>
sxkac@java.sois.alaska.edu (Kurt Carlson)

Thanks to each of them!

All of them indicated that (as I suspected) you don't need to reinstall DU
if you're already running a recent enough version.  Kurt and Alan confirmed
my suspicion that the biggest possible "gotcha" is if devices "move" after
the upgrade.  Being careful to note what slots are currently occupied in
our 2100s and placing cards in the equivalent spots in the 2100A will increase
the chances of a smooth upgrade.

A full kernel rebuild after booting from the generic kernel is a Really Good
Idea (TM) too, to make sure that the config file has the correct device 
entries for everything.

Kurt also echoed the upgrade manual's suggestion that I print a copy of the
settings for the firmware variables, so that it's easy to reset them after
upgrading the firmware.

Christophe indicated that the upgrade takes approximately 2 hours if the
FSE is careful.

Tim
