Thanks to all who answered very quickly,


My question was:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> after updating from version 3.2 to 3.2d-1 only root can login at the
> CDE-login.
> An user gets the message 
> Sorry, Maximum number of users already logged in.
> 
> This is strange, as we have an unlimited user-licence.
> Login from another machine makes no problems for users!
> Root can login without problems
> 
> How can I fix this problem?
> 
> 

The solution:

        All 3.2x releases use the same CDE ADK installation kit.
        However 3.2d release incorporated a patch to close a hole
        in C2 security, but it also had the side effect of breaking
        CDE login for non-root users. You'll need to get a hold of
        a dtlogin patch from your customer service rep.

(is fixed now....)


Another problem was solved by this advise:

Upgrading normally gives you two user licenses, the unlimited one you
had,
plus a two user "starter" license. Use lmf to get rid of the two user
one.

