From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Mar 06 08:29:44 1997
From: " nadia  Hashim Saad" <nadiakw () hotmail ! com>
Date: Thu, 06 Mar 1997 08:29:44 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Copy system disk
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078609810171

Hello,

I send my great thanks to whom replied with useful answers:

1. Mr. Brian O'Connor <boc@ironbark.bendigo.latrobe.edu.au>
2. Mr. Thomas Leitner <tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at>
3. Mr. Gary Barber <gbarber@telecom.ie>
4. Mr. Ian Piumarta <piumarta@prof.inria.fr>
5. Mr. Eugene Chu <chu@musp0.Jpl.Nasa.Gov>
6. Mr. Larry Church <lchurch@Centus.COM>
7. Mr. Jude T. Cruz <jude@tsi.com.my>
8. Mr. Alan Rollow <alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com>

The most clear & well guiding answer was from Mr. Brian O'Conner
as follows:

Assumptions:

  old disk rz0

  new disk is rz2 of type rz28
  /          mounted on a
  swap               on b
  /usr       mounted on g

Steps:

  MAKEDEV rz2
  disklabel -r -w rz2 rz28

  newfs /dev/rrz2a rz28
  newfs /dev/rrz2g rz28

  fsck /dev/rrz2a
  mount /dev/rz2a /mnt
  dump 0f - / | (cd /mnt; restore xf -)

  edit /mnt/etc/fstab to replace rz0 with rz2 by:
       vi /mnt/etc/fstab
       :%s/rz0/rz2/g

  if swapdefault exists, remove it and re-create it to point at the 
  new swap partition.

  umount /mnt
  fsck /dev/rrz2a

  fsck /dev/rrz2g
  mount /dev/rz2g /mnt
  dump 0f - /usr | (cd /mnt; restore xf -)

  umount /mnt
  fsck /dev/rrz2g

  shutdown and boot from the new disk

Note: You might need to recompile the kernel.
____________________________________________________________________

Mr. Thomas Leitner advised upon his own practical exercise which is
working succussful and based on ADVFS as follows:

  vdump 0uf - / | vrestore -x -D /mnt/newroot
  vdump 0uf - /usr | vrestore -x -D /mnt/newusr

  if advfs root domain exists then make sure when using disklabel to
  use the option "-t advfs" instead of "-t ufs".

____________________________________________________________________

Dear members, that was my first query through this group and I'm
indeed happy with this experiment... Thankx all.

____________________________________________________________________

Nadia Hashim Saad.
