From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Mar 05 23:42:16 1997
From: skoog () netcom ! com (Jim Skoog)
Date: Wed, 05 Mar 1997 23:42:16 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: rrestore HP<->DU
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078609810168

PROBLEM

hpux rrestore from DU3.2G TLZ06

I have a 4mm dat tape written on a DEC Alpha TLZ06, running
Digital UNIX 3.2G, which is an rdump from an HP-UX 9.05 9000/715.
The hp-ux rrestore command doesn't recognize the backup as a dump.
With dd I can access the contents of the backup.  Is there a way
to decode the contents of the tape, to undo any network data
manipulation?  The alternative is to have the bits coaxed
off a broken disk.

SOULTION

No solution.  HP-UX rdump/rrestore is only supported to and from
HP UNIX machines.  HP support found similar calls with the same
problem and no solution.  To determine why this doesn't work,
I used dump on the HP to a local disk, and I was able to restore from
the disk dump file.  The size of the root file system was 1091665920
bytes.  I used dd to extract the root file system produced by using
the HP-UX rdump to DU 3.2C and the same root files system was
4307456 bytes.  The broken disk is being rebuilt to recover the data.
                    
THANKS FOR SUGGESTIONS TO

Alan Nabeth
James Sainsbury
Allan Simeone

